cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its analysis outputs, please cite it as below."
title: "Prevalence, Thresholds, and Subgroup Performance Gaps in Clinical Prediction Models: A Multi-Dataset Analysis"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Zavashgh/clinical-prediction-subgroup-gaps"
authors:
  - family-names: Ghorbanpourbaboli
    given-names: Zavash
  - family-names: Afshar
    given-names: Arina
  - family-names: Jangravi
    given-names: Elham
  - family-names: Alaoui Mhamdi
    given-names: Mohammed Ayoub
  - family-names: Butler
    given-names: Russell
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and reference outputs for a retrospective secondary analysis of
  five publicly available clinical prediction datasets, examining within-dataset
  subgroup sensitivity differences across sex, age, and race/ethnicity, and how
  prevalence standardization and operating thresholds affect their
  interpretation. All data-derived preprocessing is fitted on training
  observations only, and the Diabetes-130 dataset is partitioned, cross-
  validated, calibrated, and resampled at the patient level.
keywords:
  - clinical prediction models
  - machine learning
  - algorithmic bias
  - health equity
  - model evaluation
